## SQ-RDB-04
@phase worldgen
@group B
@commands New world; `/place feature rusticdelight:wild_bell_peppers_placed`, `wild_cotton_placed`, `wild_coffee_placed`, `bell_pepper_block_patch_placed` on grass; a jungle temple and village chest roll (loot tables `/loot spawn`) and a Wandering Trader
@pass Patches place (peppers base colors only); chest seeds and trader seeds as in SQ-RD-24, -26
@fails `base_patch` rule or a worldgen file missing
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@absent rusticdelight:wild_bell_peppers rusticdelight:wild_cotton rusticdelight:wild_coffee rusticdelight:bell_pepper_block_patch (configured features of the CD rustic member; the registry dump lists none)
# a grass platform at y 199 far from spawn
# r1120fix (2026-11-20): /place feature takes CONFIGURED feature ids in 1.19.2 (the _placed ids are placed features) and
# answers Placed "<id>" at x, y, z (was counted as "Placed feature", which never matches)
> forceload add 41000 41000 41047 41047
> fill 41000 199 41000 41047 199 41047 minecraft:grass_block
> place feature rusticdelight:wild_bell_peppers 41008 200 41008
> place feature rusticdelight:wild_cotton 41038 200 41008
> place feature rusticdelight:wild_coffee 41008 200 41038
> place feature rusticdelight:bell_pepper_block_patch 41038 200 41038
> cdevtest count 41000 200 41000 41047 202 41047 #minecraft:replaceable_plants
> cdevtest count 41000 200 41000 41047 202 41047 rusticdelight:wild_cotton
> cdevtest count 41000 200 41000 41047 202 41047 rusticdelight:wild_coffee
> cdevtest count 41000 200 41000 41047 202 41047 rusticdelight:bell_pepper_red_block
count Placed "rusticdelight: == 4
reject Failed to place feature
expect verb=count block=rusticdelight:wild_cotton n=[1-9]
expect verb=count block=rusticdelight:wild_coffee n=[1-9]
reject verb=count block=\S+ .*on=\S*minecraft:(dirt|sand):
# chest rolls (SQ-RD-26 seeds) and a trader
repeat 40
> loot spawn 41020 201 41020 loot minecraft:chests/jungle_temple
end
> cdevtest items 41020 201 41020 3
repeat 40
> loot spawn 41020 201 41020 loot minecraft:chests/village/village_plains_house
end
> cdevtest items 41020 201 41020 3
> summon minecraft:wandering_trader 41024 200 41024 {NoAI:1b}
> data get entity @e[type=minecraft:wandering_trader,limit=1,x=41024,y=200,z=41024,distance=..3] Offers.Recipes
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
look the wild pepper patch placed its plant and the giant patch only red, yellow or green blocks (the ids in the four Placed lines); chest items lines carry the Rustic seeds as in SQ-RD-26 (rusticdelight: ids among the sums); trader offers name a rusticdelight seed or none (record)
## SQ-RDB-05 | Rustic blocks from the 1.2.02 save keep their states
@group old world
@commands Save from the live pack with Rustic plates, crops, crates and potted wild coffee (as SQ-RD-03), opened on the -02 jar
@pass Every block keeps its state; no missing-registry warning for `rusticdelight:`
@fails Ids did not change, so a loss is a registry bug, not the bake
@from batches/r1115/p9_o2.qb passed
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@superseded by SQ-UPG-12 (1.2.02 upgrade section) (owner ruling 1, 2026-11-18)
> cdevtest state 200 -60 200
> cdevtest state 202 -60 200
> cdevtest state 204 -60 200
> cdevtest state 206 -60 200
> cdevtest state 208 -60 200
> cdevtest state 210 -60 200
> cdevtest state 212 -60 200
> cdevtest state 214 -60 200
> cdevtest state 216 -60 200
> cdevtest state 218 -60 200
> cdevtest state 220 -60 200
expect verb=state pos=200,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:pancakes\[facing=east,servings=4\]"
expect verb=state pos=202,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:honey_pancakes\[facing=east,servings=7\]"
expect verb=state pos=204,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:cotton\[age=3\]"
expect verb=state pos=206,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:coffee\[age=4\]"
expect verb=state pos=208,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:bell_peppers\[age=6\]"
expect verb=state pos=210,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:bell_pepper_red_crate
expect verb=state pos=212,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:cotton_boll_crate
expect verb=state pos=214,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:potted_wild_coffee
expect verb=state pos=216,-60,200 state="rusticdelight:cherry_blossom_cheesecake\[bites=1,facing=north\]"
expect verb=state pos=218,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:wild_coffee
expect verb=state pos=220,-60,200 state=rusticdelight:glowing_calamari_crate
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ done=0
shell echo "missing-registry lines naming rusticdelight: $(grep -ciE '(missing|unidentified|unknown).*rusticdelight' logs/latest.log)"; grep -iE "(missing|unidentified|unknown).*rusticdelight" logs/latest.log | cut -c1-240 | head -8

## SQ-RDB-06 | old rustic_upstream folder beside mods/ is ignored
@group A (no old save)
@commands Boot with the old `rustic_upstream/` folder (the 1.7.0 jar) beside `mods/`: the scratch setup links the instance's folder in by default (`scratch_server.sh` links every `*_upstream`); check it is there
@pass Same as SQ-RDB-01: no duplicate pack, no error, folder ignored
@fails A pack named `rustic_upstream_assets` in the pack list: an old jar still nested. The folder check fails: the scratch setup no longer links `*_upstream` folders (then add `@@prep copy rustic_upstream rustic_upstream`)
@from batches/r1111/a2.qb
# r1118 R3 (2026-11-18): rewritten for any world (no second boot): the default scratch setup already has the folder
bootexpect Done \(
bootreject (?i)(Couldn't parse|Failed to load).*rusticdelight:
bootreject rustic_upstream_assets
# grep -c exits 1 on 0 matches, the good outcome here (judge-11, 2026-11-18)
shell test -e rustic_upstream/rusticdelight-forge-1.20.1-1.7.0.jar || { echo "rustic_upstream missing: the row did not test the folder"; exit 1; }; echo "rustic error lines: $(grep -iE 'rustic' logs/latest.log | grep -ciE "error|exception|couldn't parse|failed to load")"

## CQ-RDB-01
@group client
@commands Creative tab and JEI for Rustic: peppers (nine colours), pancake plates, syrup, coffee, cotton; place each flavoured pancake on a Brewin' coaster; hover items with FD tooltips (syrup, pumpkin, cherry blossom tea)
@pass LOOK: textures and names as before; the six pancake recolours (as in 1.2.02); coaster pancakes render (no magenta cube); `grep "coaster/pancake" logs/latest.log` empty
@fails Missing texture: `bake_upstream.py --check`; recolour lost: `own_overrides.json`
@reviewed 2026-11-16
do {"tooltip_text": "rusticdelight:syrup", "reject": "rusticdelight\\.\\w|item\\.rusticdelight"}
do {"tooltip_text": "rusticdelight:pancakes", "reject": "item\\.rusticdelight"}
> fill 0 100 0 8 100 2 minecraft:stone
> setblock 0 101 1 rusticdelight:pancakes
> setblock 2 101 1 rusticdelight:honey_pancakes
> setblock 4 101 1 brewinandchewin:coaster
do {"wait": "jei"}
do {"screen": "creative:rusticdelight"}
shot creative_tab
do {"screen": "close"}
do {"look": {"from": "2 103 -2", "at": "2 101 1"}}
do {"wait": "chunks"}
shot placed
shell grep -c "coaster/pancake" logs/latest.log; true
look textures and names as before, the six pancake recolours, coaster pancakes (place each flavoured pancake on the coaster by hand) render without a magenta cube; the grep count 0

