## SQ-RDB-01 | Rustic Delight with no rustic_upstream folder
@group A
@commands Boot with no `rustic_upstream/` folder (and no symlink) in the server dir; `grep -i "rustic\|Error occurred while handling event\|Couldn't parse\|Failed to load" logs/latest.log`
@pass `Done (`; no Rustic error or parse error for a `rusticdelight:` file; `/dumpall` items_by_mod/rusticdelight.json lists the same ids as the baseline (160 port ids plus blocks)
@fails A missing file: `bake_upstream.py --check`; a parse error: the bake rule for that folder
@from batches/r1111/a1.qb passed
# r1118 R4 (2026-11-18): own section with @@prep rm rustic_upstream (the setup links the folder by default; SQ-RDB-06 needs it there)
bootexpect Done \(
shell ls -d rustic_upstream 2>&1; grep -iE "rustic" logs/latest.log | grep -iE "error|exception|couldn't parse|failed to load" | head -20; echo "rustic error lines: $(grep -iE 'rustic' logs/latest.log | grep -ciE "error|exception|couldn't parse|failed to load")" 
bootreject (?i)(Couldn't parse|Failed to load).*rusticdelight:
